On 4/19/07, ANDREW PIEKARSKI <totus@rogers.com> wrote:
But why {...tezu'e lenu penmi le ctuca be ri} as opposed to {...tezu'e lenu penmi le ri ctuca
}?

{ le ri ctuca } expands to { le ctuca pe ri }. { le ctuca be ri } is more precise, as it picks up the x2 of {ctuca}. I agree with filip that the gismu places should be used whenever possible. mu'o mi'e komfo,amonan
